    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d737">

                <pb facs="0234" n="1284" sameAs="frus:frus1952-54v11p2/pg1284"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">690D.91/8–552: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Embassy in India</hi><anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d737-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1952-08-12T18:08:00-04:00">August 12, 1952—6:08
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>422. Dept believes it wld be desirable in ur
                    discretion informally indicate govt to which accredited that you have recd
                        msg from ur govt expressing its
                    gratification that two govts have decided send mins to meet with Graham in Geneva and its earnest hope mtg may
                    have fruitful result. Re Karachi tel 173 Aug 5 rptd New Delhi 28 and New Delhi
                    tel 562 Aug 8 rptd Karachi 24.</p>
                <p>Dept believes failure express views along above
                    line might lead misunderstanding US attitude toward Geneva mtg.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Acheson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d737-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d737-f1-content">
                <p>This telegram was repeated as telegram 239 to Karachi and for information to
                    London and New York.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
